From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koyu <me@koyu.space>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:19:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Add a web browser page

After the updates page, offers the browsers on the Forge browser list
(the one the Arc Store shows) as radio buttons. The chosen one is
installed right away and becomes the new user's default browser in
mimeapps.list and kdeglobals, then the other browsers on the list are
removed, one after another. They are system-wide Flatpaks, installed
through libflatpak, since the setup user's home doesn't survive setup.
If the chosen browser can't be installed, the others are kept. Setup
only goes on with a browser chosen; with exactly one installed already,
that one is.

Like the updates page, it is skipped without an internet connection.
The setup user may install Flatpak apps and runtimes, and remove apps,
without asking.
In a preview installs are simulated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
